node.doctext:
I remember we've discussed [metamod://Time::Piece] and timezones here. I can't find it anymore (maybe most of it was ChatterBox), but I took two lessons from it:
<ul><li>If you want the object to know about timezones, use <c>localtime</c> (see below);
<li>If you want to work with timezones, don't use Time::Piece.
</ul><P>

<c>
#! /usr/bin/perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw{ say };

use Time::Piece;

my $pattern = "%a, %d %b %Y %T";
my $str = 'Wed, 13 Jan 2021 17:22:23';

local $ENV{TZ} = 'CST';
my $u1 = Time::Piece->strptime($str, $pattern);
my $u2 = localtime($u1);
say $_->strftime('%F %T %Z') for $u1, $u2;

__END__
2021-01-13 17:22:23 UTC
2021-01-13 17:22:23 CST
</c>
